  clock: 2  # 6765
  nonce: '6765'  # 6765
  message: "Fixed alongside WI-sidot. Behavioural evidence, re-run just now rather than recalled: with the brace-group form, a real auto-pr run in a fake repo (AUTO_PR_SIMULATE_OUTAGE=1) prints '🧽 brand scrub: removed 1 line(s) from the PR body' on stderr and exits 0; before the fix the same run printed nothing on stderr at all while still scrubbing the line. The descriptor is unaffected: FD allocates (11) and 'flock -x -n $FD' succeeds. Analogue sweep over scripts/, .githooks/ and .agent/hooks/ found 3 exec-redirect sites; the other two redirect no standard stream, so this is a singleton."  # 6765
